# Code owners.
#
# Intentionally empty for now. The catch-all rule that mapped every path to a
# single owner froze all merges the moment "Require review from Code Owners"
# was enabled, because no other maintainer's approval could satisfy the gate.
# A per-area ownership map (security/auth, CI, frontend, agent internals, with
# multiple named owners per line) is being worked out in issue #593; once
# agreed it replaces this file. Until then, the security CI gate
# (docs/security-ci.md) remains in force via branch protection on `main`.
#
# `D-2026-11-24-04`: `docs/security-ci.md` §1 tells the operator to leave
# "Require review from Code Owners" OFF and to require 0 approvals. Every pull
# request comes from the owner's own account and GitHub does not let an author
# approve their own, so a required review is a rule nobody can meet. "Require a
# pull request before merging" plus the twelve named status checks are what
# hold the line on `main`. Re-read that section before giving this file owners.
